  "body": "We've announced the deprecation of Python 3.5, intending to break compatibility no sooner than April 2021.\r\n\r\nSo here are a bunch of small tasks we can take care of when April rolls around:\r\n\r\n- [x] Bump the version of Black we use for code formatting\r\n- [x] Bump the `tool.black.target-version` in pyproject.toml\r\n- [x] Run Black on all the things\r\n- [x] Update our Trove classifiers to drop support for 3.5\r\n- [x] Update CI configuration to stop testing on 3.5\r\n- [x] Update .deb build script to stop building for Debian Stretch and Ubuntu Xenial\r\n- [x] Drop the weird build script bits around dh-systemd\r\n- [x] Drop the dependency constraints for pyjwt / pysaml\r\n- [ ] Audit our python package's extras -- I think I recall something in `[lint]` not supporting 3.5, and that complicating install / contributing docs, maybe?\r\n- [x] Announce to devs that we can finally use f'strings'\r\n- [x] Py 3.6 marked asyncio's API as stable; check if there's anywhere that would make life easier for us\r\n- [x] Py 3.6 introduced a new `secrets` module to replace `os.urandom`, see if that would make life easier for us\r\n- [x] Grep source and docs for anything referencing Python 3.5, Stretch, or Xenial and excise it\r\n- [x] Update the minimum version of unpaddedbase64 to 2.1.0 and remove its `ignore_missing_imports` line from `mypy.ini`",
